::: eye | How to revise from these notes
Never just read. For each heading of a revision sheet, **cover it, say it aloud, then check**. For each diagram, draw it on a blank sheet before you look. For each answer plan, read only the question, say the plan from memory, then compare. What you cannot recall is what you revise next. Reading feels like learning, but recalling is what you will do on the day.
:::

## The three-week timetable

The plan gives the heavy topics (T4 and T1) two days each in the first pass, then a second pass from memory, two full mock sittings, and a light final day.

